#
# PART PROGRAMMING IS BOUND AS ONE TRADE WITH TWO WORK SURFACES (owner ruling, this session).
# NCO 7223.6003 defines a CNC Programmer as producing the component program "using manual data
# input or by use of a remote computer", which is the desk CAM programmer AND the man typing
# the program into the controller. Binding only a desk reading of the role would have left
# every MDI programmer on fam_machining's six generic questions; qp_cam_programming's first
# question splits the two surfaces, the way qp_machining's machine_type splits the machine.
# One code, so one binding: 7223.6003 is the only NCO occupation in the unit whose whole
# definition is writing the program. 7223.5001 ("CNC Operator") stays on fam_machining, for
# the same reason the turner does not claim it.
{"kind":"binding","family_id":"fam_cam_programming","job_domain_id":"jd_nco_7223_6003"}
